commit 1c1d4e1876a221f54553126f3c0c5eba2785247a
Author: dong881 <minghunghsu.taiwan@gmail.com>
Date:   Thu Mar 12 19:23:43 2026 +0800

    feat(nfapi/vnf): rewrite UL node sync with NTP-style clock offset and TIMEHR wrap-around fix
    
    Fix get_slot_time() wrap-around and rewrite vnf_nr_handle_ul_node_sync()
    with a proper NTP-style bi-directional offset formula.
    
    TIMEHR wrap-around fix:
    - Add timehr_diff_us() in vnf_p7.c (mirrors the PNF helper) computing
      a signed difference that handles the 12-bit second wrap (~4096 s)
    - Rewrite get_slot_time() using timehr_diff_us instead of the broken
      ad-hoc us-only comparison
    
    UL node sync rewrite:
    - Compute clock offset using the standard NTP formula:
        offset = ((t2 - t1) - (t4 - t3)) / 2
      where t1/t4 are VNF send/receive times and t2/t3 are PNF timestamps
    - Compute one-way delay for logging
    - Convert offset to slot+us adjustment:
        slot_adjustment = (offset + TARGET_MARGIN_INITIAL) / slot_us
        us_adjustment   = (offset + TARGET_MARGIN_INITIAL) % slot_us
    - Apply adjustments via mutex to avoid race with vnf_timing_thread
    - Set sync_locked once offset converges within TARGET_MARGIN_INITIAL
    
    vnf_p7.h:
    - Add DYNAMIC SLOT SLEEP TIMING CONTROL constants (MARGIN_TOLERANCE_US,
      TARGET_MARGIN_INITIAL, TARGET_TIMING_WINDOW, MIN/MAX_SLEEP_US,
      SLOT_ARRAY_SIZE)
    - Add slot_adjustment, us_adjustment, sync_locked, sync_slot_counter,
      sync_period_slots, initial_timinginfo_received to connection_info

